
		Odds and Ends of interest

1.  Dos directory structure is not necessarily complete.  In
order to save the time required to build a full dir structure
of a device like a hard disk, and because operators usually
want to copy to or from the current directory, M2D builds only
the current Dos dir and then adds more dir structure if and
when the op moves through the structure (up or down).  This
means that the root level can change and that child pointers
MAY be empty.

2.  MacRootLevel is a fixed address and is found by using LEA. 
The DosRootLevel is a POINTER to the DosRootLevel block.  Use a
MOVE.L to get the address of the DosRootLevel block.  Watch out
- this is a GOTCHA!



